<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Finding the Percent of 200</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00070</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Finding the Percent of 200</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d2548bdf-9a30-4ee8-91aa-f96cfa793d82</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">You will be asked to evaluate the percentage of a number mentally. Sometimes, a visual is helpful to do this. If needed, use the GeoGebra activity to help you determine the requested values. Then, look for a pattern that can be used to describe how to find the percentage of any number.</para>
      
        <media alt="An interactive activity to further practice mathematical skills. Produced by Geogrebra.">
          <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.openstax.org/r/geogebra-XSFd8GkK"/>
        </media>
      
      <exercise id="_89acbc05-bc17-40cb-9872-c5ce8a7fb71f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">What is 25% of 200?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">50</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7b37d976-9dba-4f13-af94-03b694dd688f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">What is 12% of 200?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">24</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="dd65ceb4-46ec-46c7-830f-cdeeec095223" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00008">What is 8% of 200?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">16</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!-- Q4 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00011">How would you determine <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>% of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>200</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00012"/>
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></item>
            <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>200</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
            <item>Change the percentage to a decimal and multiply it by 200.</item>
            <item>Since percent means “per hundred” and there are two hundreds, the percentage is multiplied by two.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!-- Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>